# wishbusterz-rider — optional API keys.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. Six offline domains and the `live` domain need
# nothing at all — copy this file only if you want measured PageSpeed scores or
# the Google registration checks.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    (.env is gitignored; never commit real keys)
#
# The tool does not read .env itself — export these into your shell, or use
# your runner's secret store. In GitHub Actions, set them as repository secrets
# (see .github/workflows/audit.yml).

# ─── Easy: measured PageSpeed / Core Web Vitals (the `lighthouse` domain) ──────
#
# A free key from the Google Cloud console — enable "PageSpeed Insights API",
# then create an API key. No billing, no OAuth, ~2 minutes:
#   https://developers.google.com/speed/docs/insights/v5/get-started
#
# Without it the lighthouse domain just ⏭ skips and everything else still runs.
# Note PSI needs a PUBLICLY REACHABLE url — it can't see localhost.
PAGESPEED_API_KEY=

# ─── Advanced: is the site registered and measured? (the `google` domain) ──────
#
# Only worth setting up if you own the Search Console / Analytics properties for
# the domain you're auditing. Needs a Google Cloud service account with the
# Search Console API, Site Verification API, and Analytics Admin API enabled,
# plus that service account granted read access to your GA account and added as
# a user on the Search Console property. Budget ~20 minutes for first-time setup.
#
# Supply the key as raw JSON (or base64 of it):
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
#
# …or point at the downloaded key file instead (Google's own convention):
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json

# The Zaraz leg of the `google` domain checks that your GA4 measurement ID is
# actually wired into Cloudflare Zaraz. Needs a Cloudflare API token with
# "Zaraz: Read" and "Zone: Read". Skips independently of the two vars above.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# ─── If you keep secrets in sops-encrypted env files ──────────────────────────
# Opt-in: point these at the encrypted file and the tool will `sops -d` the key
# out of it. Unset (the default) means this path is simply not used.
# WISHBUSTERZ_RIDER_PSI_SOPS_FILE=/path/to/secrets.enc.env
# WISHBUSTERZ_RIDER_SA_SOPS_FILE=/path/to/secrets.enc.env
